Description: growing with no scrollback keeps the rows at the top
 9.31 made a terminal that grows anchor what it shows to the bottom and move
 the cursor down by the rows it gained, even with no scrollback to pull into
 view. A terminal that a tiling window manager resizes right after it opens
 then shows its first prompt in the middle of the window (listed upstream as
 a TODO in Changes). Growing with no scrollback goes back to 9.30's way: the
 rows stay at the top and the cursor on its line. Shrinking, and growing with
 scrollback, are unchanged.
Author: minos <https://minos.io>
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-11-18
